# Domain Logic Rules

## Purity constraint

These folders contain pure TypeScript logic. Do not import from Vue, Nuxt, or any UI framework.

Allowed imports:
- npm packages (e.g. `yaml`)
- Other domain folders via `~/` alias (e.g. `import type { Note } from '~/notes/types'`)
- Same-folder files via `./` (e.g. `import { NoteStorage } from './types'`)

Forbidden imports:
- `vue`, `#app`, `#imports`, `nuxt/app`, any `@vue/*` package
- Anything from `app/components/`, `app/composables/`, `app/pages/`, `app/layouts/`

## Types

- Export explicit TypeScript types for all public interfaces.
- Prefer `type` over `interface` unless the type needs declaration merging.
- Keep types co-located with the logic that uses them (e.g. `types.ts` in the same folder).

## Testing

- Every exported function and interface implementation should have a corresponding unit test.
- Test files mirror source paths: `app/notes/parser.ts` → `tests/unit/notes/parser.test.ts`.
